IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa14-nouns`

-- coa14-ch08-alteration.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 17 Chapter 8 "Alteration of share capital", ss 617 to 628 (lines 8280-8436).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. How to read an answer: see coa14-ch07-premiums.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE with
-- a FALSE-kind comment, NOTHING with a NOTHING-kind comment). A function titled as a bar answers JUST TRUE where the text says no
-- to the act, JUST FALSE where the bar does not apply, NOTHING where the text does not decide.
-- PERIODS: "within one month after" is `add months` (calendar months: the last day is the same day of the next month, or the last
-- day of a shorter month); "within 15 days after" is the event date PLUS 15. The day of the event itself counts as in time (fork).
-- SEAMS: facts another part answers are inputs named for the answering section (s 283, s 282, s 1121, s 18 ...).

§ `Chapter 8 -- Alteration of share capital`

§§ `s 617 Alteration of share capital of limited company`

-- src:8283 | (1) A limited company having a share capital may not alter its share capital except in the following ways.
-- src:8284 | (2) The company may—
-- src:8285 | (a) increase its share capital by allotting new shares in accordance with this Part, or
-- src:8286 | (b) reduce its share capital in accordance with Chapter 10.
-- src:8287 | (3) The company may—
-- src:8288 | (a) sub-divide or consolidate all or any of its share capital in accordance with section 618, or
-- src:8289 | (b) reconvert stock into shares in accordance with section 620.
-- src:8290 | (4) The company may redenominate all or any of its shares in accordance with section 622, and may reduce its share capital in accordance with section 626 in connection with such a redenomination.
-- src:8291 | (5) Nothing in this section affects—
-- src:8292 | (a) the power of a company to purchase its own shares, or to redeem shares, in accordance with Part 18;
-- src:8293 | (b) the power of a company to purchase its own shares in pursuance of an order of the court under—
-- src:8294 | (i) section 98 (application to court to cancel resolution for re-registration as a private company),
-- src:8295 | (ii) section 721(6) (powers of court on objection to redemption or purchase of shares out of capital),
-- src:8296 | (iii) section 759 (remedial order in case of breach of prohibition of public offers by private company), or
-- src:8297 | (iv) Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice);
-- src:8298 | (c) the forfeiture of shares, or the acceptance of shares surrendered in lieu, in pursuance of the company's articles, for failure to pay any sum payable in respect of the shares;
-- src:8299 | (d) the cancellation of shares under section 662 (duty to cancel shares held by or for a public company);
-- src:8300 | (e) the power of a company—
-- src:8301 | (i) to enter into a compromise or arrangement in accordance with Part 26 or 26A (arrangements and reconstructions), or
-- src:8302 | (ii) to do anything required to comply with an order of the court on an application under that Part.
-- src:8303 | (f) the cancellation of a share warrant issued by the company and of the shares specified in it by a cancellation order or suspended cancellation order made under paragraph 6 of Schedule 4 to the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 (cancellation where share warrants not surrendered in accordance with that Schedule);
-- src:8304 | (g) the cancellation of a share warrant issued by the company and of the shares specified in it pursuant to section 1028A(2) or 1032A(2) (cancellation of share warrants on restoration of a company).
@ref s 617(1) Alteration of share capital of limited company (src:8283-8304)
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      alteration IS A `s 617(1) alteration of share capital`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 617(1) the section bars the company from altering its share capital in this way` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a limited company having a share capital`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "A limited company having a share capital"
    ELSE CONSIDER alteration's `s 617 the way the share capital is altered`
         WHEN `s 617(2)(a) increase the share capital by allotting new shares in accordance with this Part` THEN `the bar unless in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(2)(b) reduce the share capital in accordance with Chapter 10` THEN `the bar unless in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(3)(a) sub-divide or consolidate the share capital in accordance with section 618` THEN `the bar unless in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(3)(b) reconvert stock into shares in accordance with section 620` THEN `the bar unless in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(4)(a) redenominate shares in accordance with section 622` THEN `the bar unless in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(4)(b) reduce the share capital in accordance with section 626 in connection with a redenomination` THEN `the bar unless in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(5)(a) purchase or redeem shares in accordance with Part 18` THEN `not affected if in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(5)(b) purchase shares in pursuance of an order of the court under section 98, 721(6), 759 or Part 30` THEN `not affected if in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(5)(c) forfeit shares, or accept shares surrendered in lieu, in pursuance of the articles` THEN `not affected if in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(5)(d) cancel shares under section 662` THEN `not affected if in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(5)(e) compromise or arrangement under Part 26 or 26A, or compliance with a court order on an application under that Part` THEN `not affected if in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(5)(f) cancel a share warrant and its shares under paragraph 6 of Schedule 4 to the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015` THEN `not affected if in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617(5)(g) cancel a share warrant and its shares under section 1028A(2) or 1032A(2)` THEN `not affected if in accordance`
         WHEN `s 617 some other way of altering share capital` THEN
             JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not alter its share capital except in the following ways"
    WHERE
        -- (2) to (4): the ways in which the company MAY alter its share capital, each "in accordance with" a provision
        `the bar unless in accordance` MEANS
            IF alteration's `s 617 the alteration is made in accordance with the provision that names the way`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in the following ways" (the exception is met: fork F-except-met)
            ELSE JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not alter its share capital except in the following ways" (not made in accordance with the provision that names the way)
        -- (5): "Nothing in this section affects" these powers
        `not affected if in accordance` MEANS
            IF alteration's `s 617 the alteration is made in accordance with the provision that names the way`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects"
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (5) saves the power "in accordance with" the provision; a use outside it is not addressed

§§ `s 618 Sub-division or consolidation of shares`

-- src:8307 | (1) A limited company having a share capital may—
-- src:8308 | (a) sub-divide its shares, or any of them, into shares of a smaller nominal amount than its existing shares, or
-- src:8309 | (b) consolidate and divide all or any of its share capital into shares of a larger nominal amount than its existing shares.
@ref s 618(1) Sub-division or consolidation of shares: the powers (src:8307-8309)
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      change IS A `s 618(1) kind of change to shares`
      `the nominal amount of each resulting share` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal amount of the existing shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 618(1) the company may use the power to change its shares in this way` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a limited company having a share capital`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is that of "A limited company having a share capital"
    ELSE CONSIDER change
         WHEN `s 618(1)(a) sub-division into shares of a smaller nominal amount` THEN
             IF `the nominal amount of each resulting share` LESS THAN `the nominal amount of the existing shares`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (a) is a power to sub-divide "into shares of a smaller nominal amount"
         WHEN `s 618(1)(b) consolidation and division into shares of a larger nominal amount` THEN
             IF `the nominal amount of each resulting share` GREATER THAN `the nominal amount of the existing shares`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (b) is a power to consolidate and divide "into shares of a larger nominal amount"

-- src:8310 | (2) In any sub-division, consolidation or division of shares under this section, the proportion between the amount paid and the amount (if any) unpaid on each resulting share must be the same as it was in the case of the share from which that share is derived.
@ref s 618(2) Sub-division or consolidation of shares: the proportion paid to unpaid (src:8310)
GIVEN `the amount paid on the share before` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount unpaid on the share before` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid on the resulting share` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount unpaid on the resulting share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 618(2) the proportion between the amount paid and the amount unpaid is the same as before` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount paid on the share before` PLUS `the amount unpaid on the share before` AT MOST 0
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a share with nothing paid and nothing unpaid has no proportion
        IF `the amount paid on the share before` TIMES `the amount unpaid on the resulting share` EQUALS `the amount paid on the resulting share` TIMES `the amount unpaid on the share before`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the proportion between the amount paid and the amount (if any) unpaid on each resulting share must be the same as it was in the case of the share from which that share is derived" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:8311 | (3) A company may exercise a power conferred by this section only if its members have passed a resolution authorising it to do so.
@ref s 618(3) Sub-division or consolidation of shares: only if members have passed a resolution (src:8311)
GIVEN `members have passed a resolution authorising the company to exercise the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 618(3) the section bars the company from exercising the power for want of a resolution` MEANS
    IF `members have passed a resolution authorising the company to exercise the power`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if its members have passed a resolution authorising it to do so" (the "only if" is met: fork F-except-met)
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may exercise a power conferred by this section only if its members have passed a resolution authorising it to do so"

-- src:8312 | (4) A resolution under subsection (3) may authorise a company—
-- src:8313 | (a) to exercise more than one of the powers conferred by this section;
-- src:8314 | (b) to exercise a power on more than one occasion;
-- src:8315 | (c) to exercise a power at a specified time or in specified circumstances.
@ref s 618(4) Sub-division or consolidation of shares: what the resolution may authorise (src:8312-8315)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      authorises IS A `s 618(4) what the resolution authorises`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 618(4) the resolution may authorise this` MEANS
    IF NOT `the resolution is a resolution under subsection (3)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution under subsection (3) may authorise"
    ELSE CONSIDER authorises
         WHEN `s 618(4)(a) the exercise of more than one of the powers` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 618(4)(b) the exercise of a power on more than one occasion` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 618(4)(c) the exercise of a power at a specified time or in specified circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 618(4) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant names (a) to (c) and does not say "only"

-- src:8316 | (5) The company's articles may exclude or restrict the exercise of any power conferred by this section.
@ref s 618(5) Sub-division or consolidation of shares: the articles (src:8316)
GIVEN `the articles exclude or restrict the exercise of the power in the way proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 618(5) the company's articles bar the exercise of the power` MEANS
    IF `the articles exclude or restrict the exercise of the power in the way proposed`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company's articles may exclude or restrict the exercise of any power conferred by this section" (the articles do)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company's articles may exclude or restrict the exercise of any power conferred by this section" (these articles do not: fork F-articles)

-- E1 option B, gathered by hand: the power of s 618(1) with (2), (3) and (5).
-- src:8307 | (1) A limited company having a share capital may—
-- src:8308 | (a) sub-divide its shares, or any of them, into shares of a smaller nominal amount than its existing shares, or
-- src:8309 | (b) consolidate and divide all or any of its share capital into shares of a larger nominal amount than its existing shares.
-- src:8310 | (2) In any sub-division, consolidation or division of shares under this section, the proportion between the amount paid and the amount (if any) unpaid on each resulting share must be the same as it was in the case of the share from which that share is derived.
-- src:8311 | (3) A company may exercise a power conferred by this section only if its members have passed a resolution authorising it to do so.
-- src:8312 | (4) A resolution under subsection (3) may authorise a company—
-- src:8313 | (a) to exercise more than one of the powers conferred by this section;
-- src:8314 | (b) to exercise a power on more than one occasion;
-- src:8315 | (c) to exercise a power at a specified time or in specified circumstances.
-- src:8316 | (5) The company's articles may exclude or restrict the exercise of any power conferred by this section.
@ref s 618(1), (2), (3) and (5) the company may exercise the power conferred by section 618 (src:8307-8316)
GIVEN `s 618(1) the company may use the power to change its shares in this way` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 618(2) the proportion between the amount paid and the amount unpaid is the same as before` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 618(3) the section bars the company from exercising the power for want of a resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 618(5) the company's articles bar the exercise of the power` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 618 the company may exercise the power conferred by section 618` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 618(2) the proportion between the amount paid and the amount unpaid is the same as before` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the proportion ... must be the same as it was in the case of the share from which that share is derived"
        IF `s 618(3) the section bars the company from exercising the power for want of a resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if its members have passed a resolution authorising it to do so"
        IF `s 618(5) the company's articles bar the exercise of the power` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company's articles may exclude or restrict the exercise of any power conferred by this section"
        IF       `s 618(1) the company may use the power to change its shares in this way` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 618(2) the proportion between the amount paid and the amount unpaid is the same as before` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 618(3) the section bars the company from exercising the power for want of a resolution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
             AND `s 618(5) the company's articles bar the exercise of the power` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not every limb of the section is answered, or the power in subsection (1) is not shown to cover this change


§§ `s 619 Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation`

-- The statement of capital (s 619(3)): ONE rule for the six sections that require the same statement (ss 619, 621, 625, 627,
-- 644, 649); each of those sections has its own function that calls this one. The record is in coa14-nouns.l4.
-- An empty list of class entries is NOTHING: the text says "for each class of shares" and does not say what a statement of a
-- company with no shares in any class must list.
-- src:8320 | (3) The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital immediately following the exercise of the power—
-- src:8321 | (a) the total number of shares of the company,
-- src:8322 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:8323 | (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
-- src:8324 | (c) for each class of shares—
-- src:8325 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:8326 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and
-- src:8327 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class, ...
@ref s 619(3) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: the statement of capital (src:8320-8327)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 619(3) statement of capital`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 619(3) the statement of capital states what the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (      statement's `s 619(3)(a) states the total number of shares of the company`
                  AND statement's `s 619(3)(b) states the aggregate nominal value of those shares`
                  AND statement's `s 619(3)(ba) states the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares`
                  AND statement's `s 619(3) is stated with respect to the share capital at the moment the section names`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital ... (a) the total number of shares of the company, (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares, (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid"
        IF NOT (all (GIVEN e YIELD       e's `s 619(3)(c)(i) states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares of the class`
                                    AND e's `s 619(3)(c)(ii) states the total number of shares of the class`
                                    AND e's `s 619(3)(c)(iii) states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of the class`)
                    (statement's `s 619(3)(c) the entries for each class of shares`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) for each class of shares— (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares, (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class"
        IF null (statement's `s 619(3)(c) the entries for each class of shares`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what a statement lists for a company with no shares in any class
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The pounds a fine limit stands for. The Act does not state what a level on the standard scale or the statutory maximum is
-- in pounds: both are INPUTS. Only level 3 occurs in this part's ranges; another level answers NOTHING.
-- src:8332 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 619(5) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: the fine limit in pounds (src:8332)
GIVEN limit IS A `Fine limit`
      `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
      `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a fine without a stated limit has no figure
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` fraction THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` level fraction THEN
        IF level EQUALS 3
        THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the pounds of another level of the standard scale are not an input of this part
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` pounds THEN JUST pounds

-- src:8318 | (1) If a company exercises the power conferred by section 618 (sub-division or consolidation of shares) it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares affected.
@ref s 619(1) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation (src:8318)
GIVEN `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 619(1) the last day for the notice` MEANS `add months` `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618` 1

GIVEN `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 619(1) the number of days allowed for the notice` MEANS
    (Day (`s 619(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618`)) MINUS (Day `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618`)

-- src:8318 | (1) If a company exercises the power conferred by section 618 (sub-division or consolidation of shares) it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares affected.
@ref s 619(1) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: in time (src:8318)
GIVEN `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618` IS A DATE
      `the date the company gave notice to the registrar, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 619(1) the company gave notice to the registrar in time` MEANS
    `the answer on the dates`
    WHERE
        `the answer on the dates` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the company gave notice to the registrar, if it has`
            WHEN JUST given THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF given LESS THAN `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618`
                    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "after" the event and a notice given before it is not within the period
                    IF given AT MOST `s 619(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `the date being asked about` GREATER THAN `s 619(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar" (the period of 1 month has ended and nothing was given)
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period of 1 month has not ended, so the text does not yet say whether the duty is met

-- src:8318 | (1) If a company exercises the power conferred by section 618 (sub-division or consolidation of shares) it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares affected.
@ref s 619(1) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: the duty (src:8318)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 619(1) the company's duty to give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares affected` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` Company Registrar "give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares affected"
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the notice was not given within one month after the company exercised the power conferred by section 618"


-- src:8318 | (1) If a company exercises the power conferred by section 618 (sub-division or consolidation of shares) it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares affected.
@ref s 619(1) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: contents (src:8318)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the shares affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 619(1) the notice specifies the shares affected` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the shares affected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares affected" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)


-- src:8319 | (2) The notice must be accompanied by a statement of capital.
@ref s 619(2) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: accompanied (src:8319)
GIVEN `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 619(2) the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` MEANS
    IF `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be accompanied by a statement of capital" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)


-- src:8329 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:8330 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8331 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 619(4) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: default (src:8329-8331)
GIVEN requirements IS A LIST OF (MAYBE BOOLEAN)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 619(4) default is made in complying with this section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST FALSE) requirements
        THEN JUST TRUE -- a requirement of the section is not met
        IF all (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST TRUE) requirements
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section" (every requirement of the section is met)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a requirement is not yet known to be met or not met


-- src:8329 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:8330 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8331 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 619(4) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: the company (src:8329-8331)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 619(4)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `default is made in complying with this section`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether default is made is not yet known

-- src:8329 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:8330 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8331 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 619(4) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: the officer (src:8329-8331)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 619(4)(b) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `default is made in complying with this section` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every officer of the company who is in default" (the officer is not in default, as s 1121 answers)
        IF `default is made in complying with this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
