-- "the period of 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed": the 28 days from the passing day minus 28
-- to the passing day minus 1, both counted.
-- src:8364 | The day or period specified for the purposes of paragraph (a) or (b) must be within the period of 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed.
@ref s 622(3) Redenomination of share capital: the day or period must be within the 28 days before the resolution (src:8364)
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      kind IS A `s 622(3) kind of rate of exchange`
      `the day specified in the resolution` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period specified in the resolution` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period specified in the resolution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 622(3) the day or period specified is within the 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 622(3)(a) a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution` THEN `the day is within the window` `the day specified in the resolution`
    WHEN `s 622(3)(b) the average of the rates prevailing on each consecutive day of a period specified in the resolution` THEN
        IF `the first day of the period specified in the resolution` GREATER THAN `the last day of the period specified in the resolution`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a period whose first day is after its last day is not a period
        ELSE IF `the day is within the window` `the first day of the period specified in the resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the day is within the window` `the last day of the period specified in the resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be within the period of 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)
    WHEN `s 622(3) some other rate` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "the day or period specified for the purposes of paragraph (a) or (b)"
    WHERE
        `the day is within the window` d MEANS
            IF d AT LEAST (`the day the resolution is passed` MINUS 28) AND d AT MOST (`the day the resolution is passed` MINUS 1)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be within the period of 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed"

