-- src:8365 | (4) A resolution under this section may specify conditions which must be met before the redenomination takes effect.
-- src:8366 | (5) Redenomination in accordance with a resolution under this section takes effect—
-- src:8367 | (a) on the day on which the resolution is passed, or
-- src:8368 | (b) on such later day as may be determined in accordance with the resolution.
-- src:8369 | (6) A resolution under this section lapses if the redenomination for which it provides has not taken effect at the end of the period of 28 days beginning on the date on which it is passed.
-- src:8370 | (7) A company's articles may prohibit or restrict the exercise of the power conferred by this section.
@ref s 622 the company may redenominate by the resolution (src:8358-8370)
GIVEN `s 622(1) the company may redenominate its share capital` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 622(2) the conversion is made at a rate the section requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 622(3) the rate is of a kind the section allows` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 622(3) the day or period specified is within the 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 622(7) the company's articles bar the exercise of the power` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 622 the redenomination is within the section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 622(7) the company's articles bar the exercise of the power` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company's articles may prohibit or restrict the exercise of the power conferred by this section"
        IF `s 622(2) the conversion is made at a rate the section requires` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conversion must be made at an appropriate spot rate of exchange specified in the resolution"
        IF `s 622(3) the rate is of a kind the section allows` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The rate must be either— (a) ... or (b) ..."
        IF `s 622(3) the day or period specified is within the 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be within the period of 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed"
        IF       `s 622(1) the company may redenominate its share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 622(2) the conversion is made at a rate the section requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 622(3) the rate is of a kind the section allows` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 622(3) the day or period specified is within the 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 622(7) the company's articles bar the exercise of the power` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not every limb of the section is answered

§§ `s 623 Calculation of new nominal values`

-- A table: three steps, one row each. The old nominal value of every share of the class is listed; the rate is the number of
-- units of the new currency for one unit of the old currency, as the resolution specifies it (s 622(2)).
-- src:8374 | Take the aggregate of the old nominal values of all the shares of that class.
@ref s 623 Step One (src:8374)
GIVEN `the old nominal values of all the shares of that class` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 623 Step One: the aggregate of the old nominal values of all the shares of the class` MEANS
    sum `the old nominal values of all the shares of that class`

-- src:8375 | Step Two
-- src:8376 | Translate that amount into the new currency at the rate of exchange specified in the resolution.
@ref s 623 Step Two (src:8375-8376)
GIVEN `the amount from Step One` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate of exchange specified in the resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 623 Step Two: that amount translated into the new currency` MEANS
    `the amount from Step One` TIMES `the rate of exchange specified in the resolution`

-- src:8377 | Step Three
-- src:8378 | Divide that amount by the number of shares in the class.
@ref s 623 Step Three (src:8377-8378)
GIVEN `the amount from Step Two` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares in the class` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 623 Step Three: that amount divided by the number of shares in the class` MEANS
    IF `the number of shares in the class` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the amount from Step Two` DIVIDED BY `the number of shares in the class`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the steps do not say what a class with no shares calculates to

-- src:8373 | For each class of share the new nominal value of each share is calculated as follows: Step One
-- src:8374 | Take the aggregate of the old nominal values of all the shares of that class.
-- src:8375 | Step Two
-- src:8376 | Translate that amount into the new currency at the rate of exchange specified in the resolution.
-- src:8377 | Step Three
-- src:8378 | Divide that amount by the number of shares in the class.
@ref s 623 Calculation of new nominal values (src:8373-8378)
GIVEN `the old nominal values of all the shares of that class` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the rate of exchange specified in the resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 623 the new nominal value of each share of the class` MEANS
    `s 623 Step Three: that amount divided by the number of shares in the class`
        (`s 623 Step Two: that amount translated into the new currency` (`s 623 Step One: the aggregate of the old nominal values of all the shares of the class` `the old nominal values of all the shares of that class`) `the rate of exchange specified in the resolution`)
        (count `the old nominal values of all the shares of that class`)

§§ `s 624 Effect of redenomination`

-- src:8380 | (1) The redenomination of shares does not affect any rights or obligations of members under the company's constitution, or any restrictions affecting members under the company's constitution.
-- src:8381 | In particular, it does not affect entitlement to dividends (including entitlement to dividends in a particular currency), voting rights or any liability in respect of amounts unpaid on shares.
@ref s 624(1) Effect of redenomination: what it does not affect (src:8380-8381)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 624(1) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 624(1) the redenomination affects the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 624(1) a right or obligation of a member under the company's constitution` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect any rights or obligations of members under the company's constitution"
    WHEN `s 624(1) a restriction affecting a member under the company's constitution` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or any restrictions affecting members under the company's constitution"
    WHEN `s 624(1) entitlement to dividends` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it does not affect entitlement to dividends"
    WHEN `s 624(1) entitlement to dividends in a particular currency` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(including entitlement to dividends in a particular currency)"
    WHEN `s 624(1) voting rights` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it does not affect ... voting rights"
    WHEN `s 624(1) liability in respect of amounts unpaid on shares` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it does not affect ... any liability in respect of amounts unpaid on shares"
    WHEN `s 624(1) some other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names rights, obligations and restrictions under the constitution and "In particular" three of them

-- src:8382 | (2) For this purpose the company's constitution includes the terms on which any shares of the company are allotted or held.
@ref s 624(2) Effect of redenomination: the constitution includes the terms of allotment (src:8382)
GIVEN `the term is a term on which shares of the company are allotted or held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 17 the provision is part of the company's constitution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 624(2) the term is part of the company's constitution for the purposes of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the term is a term on which shares of the company are allotted or held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `s 17 the provision is part of the company's constitution` -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes" does not close the list; the keel's s 17 answer decides the rest

-- src:8383 | (3) Subject to subsection (1), references to the old nominal value of the shares in any agreement or statement, or in any deed, instrument or document, shall (unless the context otherwise requires) be read after the resolution takes effect as references to the new nominal value of the shares.
@ref s 624(3) Effect of redenomination: references to the old nominal value (src:8383)
GIVEN `the reference is in an agreement, statement, deed, instrument or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reading it as a reference to the new nominal value would affect a right, obligation or restriction protected by subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 624(3) the reference to the old nominal value is read as a reference to the new nominal value` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the reference is in an agreement, statement, deed, instrument or document`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about references "in any agreement or statement, or in any deed, instrument or document"
        IF NOT `the resolution has taken effect`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall ... be read after the resolution takes effect as references to the new nominal value" (it has not taken effect: fork F-where-unmet)
        IF `the context otherwise requires`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(unless the context otherwise requires)" (the unless is met: fork F-except-met)
        IF `reading it as a reference to the new nominal value would affect a right, obligation or restriction protected by subsection (1)`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (1)" gives subsection (1) priority and does not say what follows
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 625 Notice to registrar of redenomination`

-- src:8385 | (1) If a limited company having a share capital redenominates any of its share capital, it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redenominated.
@ref s 625(1) Notice to registrar of redenomination (src:8385)
GIVEN `the date the company redenominated its share capital` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 625(1) the last day for the notice` MEANS `add months` `the date the company redenominated its share capital` 1

GIVEN `the date the company redenominated its share capital` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 625(1) the number of days allowed for the notice` MEANS
    (Day (`s 625(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company redenominated its share capital`)) MINUS (Day `the date the company redenominated its share capital`)

-- src:8385 | (1) If a limited company having a share capital redenominates any of its share capital, it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redenominated.
@ref s 625(1) Notice to registrar of redenomination: in time (src:8385)
GIVEN `the date the company redenominated its share capital` IS A DATE
      `the date the company gave notice to the registrar, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
      `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 625(1) the company gave notice to the registrar in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a limited company having a share capital`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a limited company having a share capital redenominates any of its share capital": the duty is that of a company in that position (fork F-where-unmet)
    ELSE `the answer on the dates`
    WHERE
        `the answer on the dates` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the company gave notice to the registrar, if it has`
            WHEN JUST given THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF given LESS THAN `the date the company redenominated its share capital`
                    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "after" the event and a notice given before it is not within the period
                    IF given AT MOST `s 625(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company redenominated its share capital`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redenominated"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `the date being asked about` GREATER THAN `s 625(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company redenominated its share capital`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redenominated" (the period of 1 month has ended and nothing was given)
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period of 1 month has not ended, so the text does not yet say whether the duty is met

-- src:8385 | (1) If a limited company having a share capital redenominates any of its share capital, it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redenominated.
@ref s 625(1) Notice to registrar of redenomination: the duty (src:8385)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 625(1) the company's duty to give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redenominated` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` Company Registrar "give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redenominated"
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the notice was not given within one month after the redenomination"


-- src:8385 | (1) If a limited company having a share capital redenominates any of its share capital, it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redenominated.
@ref s 625(1) Notice to registrar of redenomination: contents (src:8385)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the shares redenominated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 625(1) the notice specifies the shares redenominated` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the shares redenominated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redenominated" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)


-- src:8387 | (a) state the date on which the resolution was passed, and
@ref s 625(2)(a) Notice to registrar of redenomination: the date of the resolution (src:8387)
GIVEN `the notice states the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 625(2)(a) the notice states the date on which the resolution was passed` MEANS
