    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must— (a) state the date on which the resolution was passed" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)


-- src:8388 | (b) be accompanied by a statement of capital.
@ref s 625(2)(b) Notice to registrar of redenomination: accompanied (src:8388)
GIVEN `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 625(2)(b) the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` MEANS
    IF `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) be accompanied by a statement of capital" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)


