        IF `s 626(2) the section bars the reduction for want of a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reduction of capital under this section requires a special resolution of the company"
        IF `s 626(3) the reduction resolution was passed in time` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be passed within three months of the resolution effecting the redenomination"
        IF `s 626(4) the amount of the reduction is within the limit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not exceed 10% of the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital immediately after the reduction"
        IF       `s 626(1) the company may reduce its share capital under this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 626(2) the section bars the reduction for want of a special resolution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
             AND `s 626(3) the reduction resolution was passed in time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `s 626(4) the amount of the reduction is within the limit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not every limb of the section is answered

§§ `s 627 Notice to registrar of reduction of capital in connection with redenomination`

-- src:8410 | (1) A company that passes a resolution under section 626 (reduction of capital in connection with redenomination) must within 15 days after the resolution is passed give notice to the registrar stating—
-- src:8411 | (a) the date of the resolution, and
-- src:8412 | (b) the date of the resolution under section 622 in connection with which it was passed.
@ref s 627(1) Notice to registrar of reduction of capital in connection with redenomination (src:8410-8412)
GIVEN `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 627(1) the last day for the notice` MEANS `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626` PLUS 15

GIVEN `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 627(1) the number of days allowed for the notice` MEANS
    (Day (`s 627(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626`)) MINUS (Day `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626`)

-- src:8410 | (1) A company that passes a resolution under section 626 (reduction of capital in connection with redenomination) must within 15 days after the resolution is passed give notice to the registrar stating—
-- src:8411 | (a) the date of the resolution, and
-- src:8412 | (b) the date of the resolution under section 622 in connection with which it was passed.
@ref s 627(1) Notice to registrar of reduction of capital in connection with redenomination: in time (src:8410-8412)
GIVEN `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626` IS A DATE
      `the date the company gave notice to the registrar, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 627(1) the company gave notice to the registrar in time` MEANS
    `the answer on the dates`
    WHERE
        `the answer on the dates` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the company gave notice to the registrar, if it has`
            WHEN JUST given THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF given LESS THAN `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626`
                    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "after" the event and a notice given before it is not within the period
                    IF given AT MOST `s 627(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that passes a resolution under section 626 ... must within 15 days after the resolution is passed give notice to the registrar"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `the date being asked about` GREATER THAN `s 627(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that passes a resolution under section 626 ... must within 15 days after the resolution is passed give notice to the registrar" (the period of 15 days has ended and nothing was given)
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period of 15 days has not ended, so the text does not yet say whether the duty is met

